{
  "title": "A Famous Dua for Sustenance",
  "data": "Dua of Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.)\nاَللّٰهُمَّ ارْزُقْنِىْ مِنْ فَضْلِكَ الْوَاسِعِ\nALLAAHUMMAR ZUQNEE MIN FADLIKAL WAASI'\nO Allah, provide me out of Your all-inclusive,\nالْحَلَالِ الطَّيِّبِ\nAL-HALAALIT TAYYIB\nlegal, and pleasant sustenance\nرِزْقًا وَاسِعًا\nRIZQAN WAASI'AA\nwith sustenance that is expansive,\nحَلَالًا طَيِّبًا\nHALAALAN TAYYIBAA\nlegally gotten, pleasant,\nبَلَاغًا لِلدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ\nBALAAGHAN LID DUNYAA WAL AAKHIRAH\ncovering all this-worldly and other-worldly demands,\nصَبًّا صَبًّا\nSABBAN SABBAA\npouring, torrential,\nهَنِيْئًا مَرِيْئًا\nHANEE'AN MAREE'AA\nenjoyable, and wholesome,\nمِنْ غَيْرِ كَدٍّ\nMIN GHAYRI KADD\nwithout exhaustive toil,\nوَلَا مَنٍّ مِّنْ اَحَدٍ مِّنْ خَلْقِكَ\nWA LAA MANNIM MIN AHADIM MIN KHALQIK\nand without the favor of any of Your creatures;\nاِلَّا سَعَةً مِّنْ فَضْلِكَ الْوَاسِعِ\nILLAA SA'ATAM MIN FADLIKAL WAASI'\nrather, with an abundance out of Your all-inclusive favors.\nفَاِنَّكَ قُلْتَ وَاسْئَلُوْا اللّٰهَ مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ\nFA-INNAKA QULTA WAS'ALULLAAHA MIN FADLIH\nfor You have said, \"Ask Allah of His grace.\"\nفَمِنْ فَضْلِكَ اَسْئَلُ\nFAMIN FADLIKA AS'AL\nThus, from Your grace only do I ask,\nوَمِنْ عَطِيَّتِكَ اَسْئَلُ\nWA MIN A'TIYYATIKA AS'AL\nfrom Your gift only do I ask,\nوَمِنْ يَدِكَ الْمَلْاَ اَسْئَلُ\nWA MIN YADIKAL MAL'A AS'AL\nand from Your abounding hand do I ask.",
  "tabs": [
    "In Prostration of an Obligatory Prayer\nIn the prostration of an obligatory prayer, recite:\nيَا خَيْرَ الْمَسْئُوْلِيْنَ وَيَا خَيْرَ الْمُعْطِيْنَ\nYAA KHAYRAL MAS'OOLEENA WA YAA KHAYRAL MU'TEEN\nO Best of those who are asked, O Best of givers,\nاُرْزُقْنِىْ وَارْزُقْ عِيَالِىْ مِنْ فَضْلِكَ\nURZUQNEE WARZUQ I'YAALEE MIN FADLIK\nprovide for me and for my family out of Your grace,\nفَاِنَّكَ ذُو الْفَضْلِ الْعَظِيْمِ\nFA-INNAKA DHUL FADLIL A'ZEEM\nfor You are the Possessor of great grace.",
    "In Prostration of the Night Prayer\nIn a prostration of the Night Prayer (Shaykh al-Tusi: the second prostration of its eighth unit), recite:\nيَا خَيْرَ مَدْعُوٍّ وَيَا خَيْرَ مَسْئُوْلٍ\nYAA KHAYRA MAD'UWWIN WA YAA KHAYRA MAS'OOL\nO Best of those called upon, O Best of those asked,\nوَيَا اَوْسَعَ مَنْ اَعْطٰى وَيَا خَيْرَ مُرْتَجِىً\nWA YAA AWSA'A MAN A'TAA WA YAA KHAYRA MURTAJAA\nO Most Generous of those who give, O Best of those hoped for,\nاُرْزُقْنِىْ وَاَوْسِعْ عَلَىَّ مِنْ رِزْقِكَ\nURZUQNEE WA AWSI' A'LAYYA MIN RIZQIK\nprovide for me and widen Your sustenance for me,\nوَسَبِّبْ لِىْ رِزْقًا مِنْ قِبَلِكَ\nWA SABBIB LEE RIZQAN MIN QIBALIK\nand make for me a means of sustenance from You;\nاِنَّكَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْئٍ قَدِيْرٌ\nINNAKA A'LAA KULLI SHAY'IN QADEER\nsurely You have power over all things.",
    "Dua of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.)\nيَا رَازِقَ الْمُقِلِّيْنَ وَيَا رَاحِمَ الْمَسَاكِيْنَ\nYAA RAAZIQAL MUQILLEENA WA YAA RAAHIMAL MASAAKEEN\nO Provider of the needy, O Merciful to the destitute,\nوَيَا وَلِىَّ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَيَا ذَا الْقُوَّةِ الْمَتِيْنَ\nWA YAA WALIYYAL MU'MINEENA WA YAA DHAL QUWWATIL MATEEN\nO Guardian of the believers, O Possessor of firm strength,\nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاَهْلِ بَيْتِهٖ\nSALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AHLI BAYTIH\nbless Muhammad and his Household,\nوَارْزُقْنِىْ وَعَافِنِىْ وَاكْفِنِىْ مَا اَهَمَّنِىْ\nWARZUQNEE WA A'AFINEE WAKFINEE MAA AHAMMANEE\nprovide for me, grant me well-being, and suffice me in what concerns me.",
    "Dua of Imam Zayn al-Abidin (a.s.)\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنّى اَسْئَلُكَ حُسْنَ الْمَعِيْشَةِ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS'ALUKA HUSNAL MA'EESHAH\nO Allah, I ask You for a good livelihood,\nمَعِيْشَةً اَتَقَوِّىْ بِهَا عَلٰى جَمِيْعِ حَوَاۤئِجِىْ\nMA'EESHATAN ATAQAWWEE BIHAA A'LAA JAMEE'I HAWAA'IJEE\na livelihood by which I gain strength for all my needs\nوَاَتَوَصَّلُ بِهَا فِى الْحَيٰوةِ اِلٰى اٰخِرَتِىْ\nWA ATAWASSALU BIHAA FIL HAYAATI ILAA AAKHIRATEE\nand by which I reach, through this life, my Hereafter,\nمِنْ غَيْرِ اَنْ تُتْرِفَنِىْ فِيْهَا فَاَطْغِىْ\nMIN GHAYRI AN TUTRIFANEE FEEHAA FA-ATGHEE\nwithout You giving me luxury in it so that I transgress,\nاَوْ تُقَتِّرَ بِهَا عَلَىَّ فَاَشْقِىْ\nAW TUQATTIRA BIHAA A'LAYYA FA-ASHQEE\nor straitening me in it so that I become wretched.\nاَوْسِعْ عَلَىَّ مِنْ حَلَالِ رِزْقِكَ\nAWSI' A'LAYYA MIN HALAALI RIZQIK\nWiden for me Your lawful sustenance,\nوَاَفْضِلْ عَلَىَّ مِنْ سَيْبِ فَضْلِكَ\nWA AFDIL A'LAYYA MIN SAYBI FADLIK\nand bestow on me from the flow of Your grace\nنِعْمَةً مِنْكَ سَابِغَةً وَعَطَاۤءً غَيْرَ مَمْنُوْنٍ\nNI'MATAN MINKA SAABIGHATAN WA A'TAA'AN GHAYRA MAMNOON\nan ample blessing from You and a gift without end.\nثُمَّ لَا تَشْغَلْنِىْ عَنْ شُكْرِ نِعْمَتِكَ\nTHUMMA LAA TASHGHALNEE A'N SHUKRI NI'MATIK\nThen do not distract me from thanking You for Your blessing\nبِاِكْثَارٍ مِنْهَا تُلْهِيْنِىْ بَهْجَتُهٗ وَتَفْتِنُنِىْ زَهَرَاتُ زَهْوَتِهٖ\nBI-IKTHAARIN MINHAA TULHEENEE BAHJATUHOO WA TAFTINUNEE ZAHARAATU ZAHWATIH\nwith an abundance of it whose splendor diverts me and whose bright blossoms tempt me,\nوَلَا بِاِقْلَالٍ عَلَىَّ مِنْهَا يَقْصُرُ بِعَمَلِىْ كَدُّهٗ وَيَمْلَاُ صَدْرِىْ هَمُّهٗ\nWA LAA BI-IQLAALIN A'LAYYA MINHAA YAQSURU BI-A'MALEE KADDUHOO WA YAMLA'U SADREE HAMMUH\nnor with a scarcity of it whose toil cuts short my deeds and whose worry fills my breast.\nاَعْطِنِىْ مِنْ ذٰلِكَ يَا اِلٰهِىْ غِنًى عَنْ شِرَارِ خَلْقِكَ\nA'TINEE MIN DHAALIKA YAA ILAAHEE GHINAN A'N SHIRAARI KHALQIK\nGive me of this, O my God, independence from the wicked among Your creation,\nوَبَلَاغًا اَنَالُ بِهٖ رِضْوَانَكَ\nWA BALAAGHAN ANAALU BIHEE RIDWAANAK\nand a sufficiency by which I attain Your good pleasure.\nوَاَعُوْذُ بِكَ يَا اِلٰهِىْ مِنْ شَرِّ الدُّنْيَا وَشَرِّ مَا فِيْهَا\nWA A'OODHU BIKA YAA ILAAHEE MIN SHARRID DUNYAA WA SHARRI MAA FEEHAA\nI seek refuge in You, O my God, from the evil of this world and the evil of what is in it.\nوَلَا تَجْعَلْ عَلَىَّ الدُّنْيَا سِجْنًا وَلَا فِرَاقَهَا عَلَىَّ حُزْنًا\nWA LAA TAJ'AL A'LAYYAD DUNYAA SIJNAN WA LAA FIRAAQAHAA A'LAYYA HUZNAA\nDo not make this world a prison for me, nor make parting from it a grief for me.\nاَخْرِجْنِىْ مِنْ فِتْنَتِهَا مَرْضِيًّا عَنِّىْ مَقْبُوْلًا فِيْهَا عَمَلِىْ\nAKHRIJNEE MIN FITNATIHAA MARDIYYAN A'NNEE MAQBOOLAN FEEHAA A'MALEE\nBring me out of its trials with You pleased with me and my deeds in it accepted,\nاِلٰى دَارِ الْحَيَوَانِ وَمَسَاكِنِ الْاَخْيَارِ\nILAA DAARIL HAYAWAANI WA MASAAKINIL AKHYAAR\nto the Abode of true life and the dwellings of the righteous,\nوَاَبْدِلْنِىْ بِالدُّنْيَا الْفَانِيَةِ نَعِيْمَ الدَّارِ الْبَاقِيَةِ\nWA ABDILNEE BID DUNYAL FAANIYATI NA'EEMAD DAARIL BAAQIYAH\nand give me, in place of the passing world, the bliss of the everlasting abode.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّىْ اَعُوْذُ بِكَ مِنْ اَزْلِهَا وَزِلْزَالِهَا\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE A'OODHU BIKA MIN AZLIHAA WA ZILZAALIHAA\nO Allah, I seek refuge in You from its hardship and its upheavals,\nوَمِنْ سَطَوَاتِ شَيَاطِيْنِهَا وَسَلَاطِيْنِهَا وَنَكَالِهَا\nWA MIN SATAWAATI SHAYAATEENIHAA WA SALAATEENIHAA WA NAKAALIHAA\nfrom the assaults of its devils, its rulers and their punishment,\nوَمِنْ بَغْىِ مَنْ بَغِىْ عَلَىَّ فِيْهَا\nWA MIN BAGHYI MAN BAGHEE A'LAYYA FEEHAA\nand from the oppression of whoever oppresses me in it.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ مَنْ كَادَنِىْ فَكِدْهُ\nALLAAHUMMA MAN KAADANEE FAKID-H\nO Allah, whoever plots against me, plot against him,\nوَمَنْ اَرَادَنِىْ فَاَرِدْهُ\nWA MAN ARAADANEE FA-ARID-H\nand whoever intends harm for me, intend the same for him.\nوَفُلَّ عَنِّىْ حَدَّ مَنْ نَصَبَ لِىْ حَدَّهٗ\nWA FULLA A'NNEE HADDA MAN NASABA LEE HADDAH\nBlunt for me the edge of whoever has sharpened his edge against me,\nوَاَطْفِءْ عَنِّىْ نَارَ مَنْ شَبَّ لِىْ وَقُوْدَهٗ\nWA ATFI' A'NNEE NAARA MAN SHABBA LEE WAQOODAH\nput out for me the fire of whoever has kindled its fuel against me,\nوَاكْفِنِىْ مَكْرَ الْمَكَرَةِ\nWAKFINEE MAKRAL MAKARAH\nsuffice me against the scheming of the schemers,\nوَافْقَاْ عَنِّىْ عُيُوْنَ الْكَفَرَةِ\nWAFQA' A'NNEE U'YOONAL KAFARAH\nblind the eyes of the unbelievers to me,\nوَاكْفِنِىْ هَمَّ مَنْ اَدْخَلَ عَلَىَّ هَمَّهٗ\nWAKFINEE HAMMA MAN ADKHALA A'LAYYA HAMMAH\nsuffice me against the worry of whoever brings his worry upon me,\nوَادْفَعْ عَنِّىْ شَرَّ الْحَسَدَةِ\nWADFA' A'NNEE SHARRAL HASADAH\nward off from me the evil of the envious,\nوَاعْصِمْنِىْ مِنْ ذٰلِكَ بِالسَّكِيْنَةِ\nWA'SIMNEE MIN DHAALIKA BIS SAKEENAH\nand protect me from all that with tranquility.\nوَاَلْبِسْنِىْ دِرْعَكَ الْحَصِيْنَةَ\nWA ALBISNEE DIR'AKAL HASEENAH\nClothe me in Your fortified armor,\nوَاَحْيِنِىْ فِىْ سِتْرِكَ الْوَاقِىْ\nWA AHYINEE FEE SITRIKAL WAAQEE\nkeep me alive within Your protecting cover,\nوَاَصْلِحْ لِىْ حَالِىْ وَصَدِّقْ قَوْلِىْ بِفِعَالِىْ\nWA ASLIH LEE HAALEE WA SADDIQ QAWLEE BIFI'AALEE\nset right my state, make my deeds confirm my words,\nوَبَارِكْ لِىْ فِىْ اَهْلِىْ وَمَالِىْ\nWA BAARIK LEE FEE AHLEE WA MAALEE\nand bless me in my family and my wealth."
  ],
  "merits": "Dua of Imam al-Sadiq: Mu’awiyah ibn ‘Ammar has reported: I once asked Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) to teach me a supplication for more sustenance. He therefore taught me a supplication that I have never seen more effective than it.\n\nIn prostration of an obligatory prayer: Imam al-Baqir (a.s.) is reported to have said to Zayd al-Shahham: For sustenance, you may say this supplication in the obligatory prayer while you are in the position of prostration.\n\nIn prostration of the Night Prayer: Abu-Basir is reported to have said: I complained to Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) about poverty and asked him to teach me a supplication for sustenance. He therefore taught me a supplication after which I have never needed anything. The Imam (a.s.) instructed me to say it in the Night Prayer while I am in the position of prostration. Shaykh al-Tusi, in his book Misbah al-Mutahajjid, has mentioned that it may be said in the second prostration of the eighth unit of the Night Prayer.\n\nDua of the Holy Prophet: The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) is reported to have instructed that this supplication might be said for asking for sustenance.\n\nDua of Imam Zayn al-Abidin: Abu-Basir reported this supplication for seeking sustenance from Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.), and added that Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) ascribed it to Imam ‘Ali ibn al-Husayn (a.s.)."
}
